G266.b:
⟪ἁμαρτία⟫, -ας, ἡ
(< ἁμαρτάνω, q.v.), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨חַטָּאת⁩ and cogn. forms, also for ⁨פֶּשַׁע ,עָוֹן⁩, etc.;] prop. ⟪a missing the mark⟫; in cl. (v. reff. to CR in MM, VGT, s.v.);
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪guilt⟫, ⟪sin⟫ (Plat., Arist., al.);
⟪(b)⟫ more freq., from Æsch. down, ⟪a fault, failure⟫. In NT (as LXX) always in ethical sense;
⟪1.⟫ as a principle and quality of action, = τὸ ἁμαρτάνειν, ⟪a sinning, sin⟫: ⟦Romans 5:12|Ro 5:12⟧, ⟦Romans 5:13|13⟧ ⟦Romans 5:20|20⟧; ὑφ’ ἁμαρτίαν εἶναι, ⟦Romans 3:9|Ro 3:9⟧; ἐπιμένειν, ⟦Romans 6:1|Ro 6:1⟧; ἀποθνήσκειν, νεκρὸν εἶναι τῇ ἁ., ⟦Romans 6:2|Ro 6:2⟧, ⟦Romans 6:11|11⟧; τὴν ἀ. γινώσκειν, ⟦Romans 7:7|Ro 7:7⟧; σῶμα τῆς ἁ., ⟦Romans 6:6|Ro 6:6⟧; ἀπάτη τῆς ἁ., ⟦Hebrews 3:13|He 3:13⟧; personified as a ruling principle, ἁ. βασιλεύει, κυριεύει, etc., ⟦Romans 5:21|Ro 5:21⟧ ⟦Romans 6:12|6:12⟧, ⟦Romans 6:14|14⟧ ⟦Romans 7:17|7:17⟧, ⟦Romans 7:20|20⟧; δουλεύειν, ⟦Romans 6:6|Ro 6:6⟧; δοῦλος τῆς ἁ., ⟦Romans 6:17|ib. 17⟧; νόμος τῆς ἁ., ⟦Romans 7:23|Ro 7:23⟧ ⟦Romans 8:2|8:2⟧; δύναμις τῆς ἁ., ⟦1 Corinthians 15:56|I Co 15:56⟧ (cf. ⟦Genesis 4:7|Ge 4:7⟧).
⟪2.⟫ As a generic term (disting. fr. the specific terms ἁμάρτημα, q.v., etc.) for concrete wrongdoing, violation of the divine law, ⟪sin⟫: ⟦John 8:46|Jo 8:46⟧, ⟦James 1:15|Ja 1:15⟧, al.; ποιεῖν (τὴν) ἁ., ⟦John 8:34|Jo 8:34⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:7|II Co 11:7⟧, ⟦1 John 3:8|I Jo 3:8⟧; εἴχειν ἁ., ⟦John 9:41|Jo 9:41⟧ ⟦John 15:22|15:22⟧, ⟦John 15:24|24⟧ ⟦John 19:11|19:11⟧, ⟦1 John 1:8|I Jo 1:8⟧; in pl. ἁμαρτίαι, sin in the aggregate, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:16|I Th 2:16⟧ (v. Milligan, in l.); ποιεῖν ἁμαρτίας, ⟦James 5:15|Ja 5:15⟧; πλῆθος ἁμαρτιῶν, ⟦James 5:20|Ja 5:20⟧, ⟦1 Peter 4:8|I Pe 4:8⟧; ἄφεσις ἁμαρτιῶν, ⟦Matthew 26:28|Mt 26:28⟧, ⟦Mark 1:4|Mk 1:4⟧, al.; ἐν ἁμαρτίαις εἶναι, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:17|I Co 15:17⟧; collectively, αἴρειν τὴν ἁ. τ. κόσμου, ⟦John 1:29|Jo 1:29⟧; ἀποθνήσκειν ἐν τῇ ἁ., ⟦John 8:21|Jo 8:21⟧.
⟪3.⟫ = ἁμάρτημα, ⟪a sinful deed⟫, ⟪a sin⟫: ⟦Matthew 12:31|Mt 12:31⟧, ⟦Acts 7:60|Ac 7:60⟧, ⟦1 John 5:16|I Jo 5:16⟧.
SYN.: v.s. ἁμάρτημα.

G292.b:
⟪ἀμύνω⟫,
[in LXX (mid.): ⟦Joshua 10:13|Jos 10:13⟧ (⁨נקם⁩), ⁨נָקַם⁩), ⟦Psalms 118:12|Ps 118:10-12⟧ ⁨מוּל⁩ hi.), ⟦Isaiah 59:16|Is 59:16⟧ (⁨ישׁע⁩ hi.), Wi 11:3, al.;] ⟪to ward off⟫, etc. Mid.
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to defend oneself against⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to requite⟫;
⟪(c)⟫ = act., ⟪to defend⟫, ⟪assist⟫ (⟦Isaiah 59:16|Is 59:16⟧): c. acc. pers., ⟦Acts 7:24|Ac 7:24⟧ (MM, VGT, s.v.).†
